## 6. User Experience & Interfaces

### 6.1 Web Management Interface
- **Dashboard:** Real-time threat monitoring and system status
- **Detection Rules:** Configure algorithms and thresholds
- **Incident Management:** Review, analyze, and respond to detections
- **Reporting:** Generate compliance and security reports
- **Administration:** User management, system configuration

### 6.2 Command Line Interface (CLI)
```bash
# Detection operations
stegox detect --input image.png --algorithms all --threshold medium
stegox scan --directory /uploads --recursive --output report.json

# Encoding/decoding operations
stegox encode --cover image.png --payload secret.txt --output stego.png --algorithm lsb --depth 2
stegox decode --input stego.png --output extracted.txt --password secret

# Network monitoring
stegox monitor --interface eth0 --block-level high --log-file network.log
stegox policy --create "Block High Risk" --threshold 0.8 --action quarantine
```

### 6.3 REST API
```
POST /api/v1/detect           - Submit file for analysis
GET  /api/v1/status           - System health and statistics
POST /api/v1/rules            - Create/update detection rules
GET  /api/v1/incidents        - Retrieve detection incidents
POST /api/v1/block            - Manual block/unblock operations
GET  /api/v1/reports          - Generate and download reports
